B.Aq=new A.bq(B.a2T,["Store sealed drinking water. The three-day baseline is 10 litres per person in total; allow extra for pets, heat, medical needs and longer isolation.","Pack non-perishable food for three days that your household normally eats, including dietary and baby needs. Include a manual can opener and utensils. No fixed food weight suits everyone.","Include essential medication, prescriptions and required medical equipment. Check storage and supply needs with a pharmacist; do not change prescribed doses.","Pack a first-aid kit suitable for your household and check its contents and expiry dates.","Have a torch or headlamp for each person where possible, a battery-powered radio and matching spare batteries.","Pack phone cables, chargers and charged power banks compatible with the phones you use.","Examples: driver licence or other ID, Medicare card, passports, birth certificates, insurance details, emergency contacts and your plan. Keep copies protected from water; no document upload is needed here.","Pack practical protective clothing, sturdy shoes, hygiene products and bedding appropriate to local conditions.","Include items for babies, disability or communication needs and personal comfort; use the pet checks below when you have pets.","Confirm that both places can receive your household. A planned place is not confirmation that an evacuation centre is open.","Confirm each vehicle, driver and usable seat. Include child restraints and mobility needs; do not count the same seat or driver twice.","Confirm how anyone without transport or needing assistance will travel.","Choose a place to reunite if separated and record a contact who can help.","Use official local warnings, road information and instructions. These planning choices do not provide safe-route guidance.","Identify outside hazards while conditions are safe. Avoid powerlines, floodwater and other dangerous areas.","Identify items that need securing before severe weather, only when it is safe to do so.","Keep access paths and exits clear and consider mobility needs.","Identify extra tasks appropriate to the hazards affecting your dwelling.","Confirm that everyone knows their preparation tasks. Do not delay evacuation to finish them.","Check unfinished tasks and requests for help before recording the review.","Discuss the plan in a way every household member can understand.","Recheck arrangements when people, transport, destinations or emergency conditions change."],t.l)
